From 37b44683b96f0e9982aca1dabf65857c43f50b0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:27:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 59/85] fix(backends): refuse --host and --weight-cache in
 tflite/executorch args

tflite_args and executorch_args come from the /load request body. Both
engines accept --host, so a request could bind the engine to the LAN
outside lemond's API key, and --weight-cache could point the engine's
cache write anywhere. Reserve both flags, as litert already reserves
--host.

Also from the F2 review: tflite and litert load failures are now
non-retryable (evicting other models cannot fix a CPU engine), tflite
no longer relaunches an engine the OOM killer stopped, and
/images/classify sorts scores and keeps the highest per label instead
of trusting the backend's order.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
